While this early return correctly handles precomputed embeddings, it is safer to ensure that the features are flattened to 2D before concatenation. Pixtral supports variable image sizes, and if multiple images are provided in a single request as separate `MultimodalDataItem`s with 3D features `(1, S_i, D)`, a direct `torch.cat` on the default dimension (0) will fail if the sequence lengths `S_i` differ. Flattening to `(S_i, D)` ensures a robust concatenation into a single sequence `(Total_S, D)`.

```suggestion
        if items and items[0].format == MultimodalInputFormat.PRECOMPUTED_EMBEDDING:
            return torch.cat([item.feature.view(-1, item.feature.shape[-1]) for item in items], dim=0)
```

